WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.820
At least 29 are dead and 48 missing after Russia bombed a Ukrainian aid site. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 42. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After this, Americans are voting on Congress. US forces have hit an Iranian island while talks continue, and Washington has moved to end a trade preference for two African countries. Later, the case on both sides of that trade decision and a sign of progress from Poland. The Guardian reports the bombs fell on Kamishivaka.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.180
A village in southern Zaporizha, hitting an AIDS center and a shelter next to it.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:39.280
President Vladimir Zelensky said Russia sent 289 attack drones, 17 ballistic missiles

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.920
and 59 cruise missiles across nine regions, and that emergency power cuts followed.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.680
He said the barrage landed as Americans' vote and that Moscow thinks Washington will miss

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:49.160
the signal.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.640
His ask was air defense, or the missile strikes do not stop.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.820
The guided bomb struck a school used to hand out aid, then the shelter nearby.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.000
high.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.560
Mikhailo Semakin, acting head of the regional military administration, said four police officers

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.060
and two rescue workers were among the dead, at least five people were hurt, and Russian

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.260
drones hit the area again on Monday evening while rescuers worked.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:16.000
In Karkeev, local authorities said a missile and drone attack wounded at least 62 people damaged

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.920
a medical facility in the Nemishlionsky district, broke windows and four apartment blocks and hit

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:21.260
cars.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.880
Ola Sinehubov said more than 200 patients were moved.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.160
Around Deneepro, local authorities said one person was killed and 17 wounded, and on

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.160
Tuesday morning, rescuers pulled a woman out of the rubble alive.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.580
After dark in Kamushyvaka, crews searched collapsed buildings with torches.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:42.560
Zelensky called the strike vile and said it shows Vladimir Putin does not want to ease the

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:42.820
fighting.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.360
He said people still in the village collect aid packages there every week, and that Moscow

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.500
Moscow chose killing over extending last week's cease-fire in Russian-occupied Oleshky,

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.480
a pause brokered by U.S. First Lady Melania Trump.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.580
The Kremlin said no similar mission is planned at the moment.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.320
That Oleshky pause was the longest of a war now in its fifth year, a war that has killed

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.340
hundreds of thousands and displaced millions.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.420
U.S. special envoy Steve Whitkopf said talks led by Washington are set for the 10th and

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.180
11th of November in Abu Dhabi.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.160
The Guardian also reported that Kiev and European allies worry Donald Trump has moved closer

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:21.632
to Moscow. Voters in the United States started casting ballots on Tuesday in midterms that

00:02:21.632 --> 00:02:25.632
decide which party runs Congress for the last two years of President Trump's second term.

00:02:26.152 --> 00:02:29.472
The New York Times has that account, and the Guardian adds the arithmetic.

00:02:30.012 --> 00:02:34.832
Every one of the 435 voting house seats is up. Republicans hold a narrow majority,

00:02:35.232 --> 00:02:40.092
and Democrats need a net gain of four seats to take the chamber. 35 Senate seats are on the ballot.

00:02:40.512 --> 00:02:45.732
33 regular and two specials in Florida and Ohio. Republicans hold 53 Senate seats.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:50.792
Democrats and Independents who sit with them hold 47, and Democrats need four more for

00:02:50.792 --> 00:02:51.272
a majority.

00:02:51.872 --> 00:02:56.372
Governors are being chosen in 36 states and three U.S. territories, along with thousands

00:02:56.372 --> 00:03:00.652
of state legislative seats and measures on taxes, abortion rights, and voting rules.

00:03:01.092 --> 00:03:05.292
The Times reported that Trump has told supporters to treat the day as if his own name is on the

00:03:05.292 --> 00:03:08.552
ballot, and that he has said Republicans win if his base shows up.

00:03:09.032 --> 00:03:13.532
Democratic campaigns have blamed his policies for household strain, and Republicans have tried

00:03:13.532 --> 00:03:17.072
to make the contest a choice against opponents they call Radical and Far Left.

00:03:17.712 --> 00:03:22.152
A New York Times and Sienna University poll published on Sunday put Democratic candidates

00:03:22.152 --> 00:03:27.272
ahead in five of seven battleground contests, including Texas and Kansas, states that last

00:03:27.272 --> 00:03:30.412
send a Democrat to the Senate in 1988 and 1932.

00:03:30.952 --> 00:03:32.912
That is a poll snapshot, not a result.

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:38.072
Early voting has broken recent midterm records, the Times reported, with more than tens of

00:03:38.072 --> 00:03:42.612
millions of ballots already in, turnout above the last midterm cycle in every major Senate

00:03:42.612 --> 00:03:47.372
battleground, and a larger share of registered Democrats in the early vote in several key states.

00:03:47.792 --> 00:03:52.632
Add-impact figures cited by the Times make this the most expensive midterm and political advertising

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:59.312
since at least 2018. Elon Musk put $474 million behind Republican candidates and their allies,

00:03:59.712 --> 00:04:05.072
more than any donor has spent in one cycle. In Michigan, Democratic Congresswoman Haley Stevens

00:04:05.072 --> 00:04:10.872
beaten by Abdul El Sayed in her party Senate primary, endorsed Republican Mike Rogers on Sunday.

00:04:10.872 --> 00:04:16.232
The president's party has lost house seats in 18 of the past 20 midterms, and 90 percent

00:04:16.232 --> 00:04:17.752
rate back to 1946.

00:04:18.452 --> 00:04:22.592
The first polls close at seven in the evening Eastern, and the time set a full count can

00:04:22.592 --> 00:04:23.512
take days or weeks.

00:04:24.032 --> 00:04:29.292
In Texas, the Texas Tribune reported, domestic male ballots postmarked by Election Day count

00:04:29.292 --> 00:04:33.772
if they arrive by five in the afternoon on the 4th of November, and military and overseas

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:37.092
ballots must be postmarked by Election Day and in by the 9th.

00:04:37.092 --> 00:04:42.677
U.S. forces struck Iran's Kesham Island late on Monday, the first hit there since June,

00:04:42.997 --> 00:04:46.277
in what officials called a defensive step, Al-Jazeera reports.

00:04:46.837 --> 00:04:51.397
Iran's IRNA said the blast came fast and that witnesses saw two planes over the island,

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.957
off the southern coast beside the Strait of Hormuz.

00:04:54.357 --> 00:04:59.017
The Wall Street Journal, quoting an unnamed official, said the strikes looked limited and were

00:04:59.017 --> 00:05:00.797
not the restart of a major operation.

00:05:01.317 --> 00:05:06.377
France 24, citing that paper and unnamed U.S. officials, called the strike on the Straits'

00:05:06.377 --> 00:05:10.177
This largest island, the latest in a run of limited hits Washington has carried out in

00:05:10.177 --> 00:05:14.077
secret in recent weeks, even as President Trump signaled progress in talks.

00:05:14.657 --> 00:05:19.237
The Associated Press quoted an unnamed U.S. official who said Washington struck Iranians

00:05:19.237 --> 00:05:21.597
using surface-to-air missiles against U.S. assets.

00:05:22.237 --> 00:05:27.197
IRNA reported that the Revolutionary Guard destroyed a U.S. MQ-9 drone east of the street.

00:05:27.677 --> 00:05:31.337
The strikes came as Vice President JD Vance described progress in the talks.

00:05:31.337 --> 00:05:36.017
This war opened on the 28th of February, when the United States and Israel struck

00:05:36.017 --> 00:05:41.297
across Iran, the straight closed, oil and gas prices jumped, and military civilian and

00:05:41.297 --> 00:05:45.457
energy sites around the Gulf were hit. On the 7th of March, the United States struck

00:05:45.457 --> 00:05:50.857
a desalination plant on Kashm. Tehran called that a flagrant crime against civilians. Fresh

00:05:50.857 --> 00:05:56.177
water to 30 villages was cut. Qatar has been passing messages. Those indirect talks looked

00:05:56.177 --> 00:06:00.757
finished on Monday, with no breakthrough. An official briefed on the talks told Reuters

00:06:00.757 --> 00:06:05.437
that Iran's delegation left Doha on Sunday with a draft still moving, and that Katari

00:06:05.437 --> 00:06:09.717
mediators flew to Tehran on Monday night to see Foreign Minister Abbas Arakji about

00:06:09.717 --> 00:06:11.457
a text negotiated for eight days.

00:06:12.097 --> 00:06:17.197
Arakji told IRNA that mediator consultations are very intensive, that Iran has put its

00:06:17.197 --> 00:06:21.257
conditions and proposals on the table, and that everything depends on what he called the

00:06:21.257 --> 00:06:22.997
political rationality of Washington.

00:06:23.777 --> 00:06:28.057
Spokesperson Esmail Bagai said the ball is in the American court, that Iran's demands

00:06:28.057 --> 00:06:32.297
are clear and logical, and that a September plan could be shortened and done in two days,

00:06:32.677 --> 00:06:37.577
including reopening hormones and going back to nuclear talks. President Mesud Peseschian

00:06:37.577 --> 00:06:41.977
said Supreme Leader Ayatollah Mojtaba Khamenei had given the government certain authorities

00:06:41.977 --> 00:06:47.736
over talks with the United States, and that Tehran would seek dialogue. President Donald Trump has

00:06:47.736 --> 00:06:52.656
told Congress he intends to take South Africa and Rwanda out of the African Growth and Opportunity

00:06:52.656 --> 00:06:58.536
Act from the first of January 2027, the BBC reports. That law lets eligible African

00:06:58.536 --> 00:07:01.736
countries sent thousands of products into the United States without duty.

00:07:02.356 --> 00:07:06.496
Trade representative Jamison Greer said a yearly review found practices that do not

00:07:06.496 --> 00:07:10.236
meet the eligibility rules that both governments were told and that the

00:07:10.236 --> 00:07:13.036
administration wants African partners to meet the criteria.

00:07:13.656 --> 00:07:17.776
Washington cited barriers to U.S. trade and investment plus national security

00:07:17.776 --> 00:07:21.496
and foreign policy concerns. For South Africa it pointed to corruption.

00:07:22.555 --> 00:07:25.455
In a letter to President Cyril Remaphosa, Trump said

00:07:25.455 --> 00:07:29.575
Pretoria's security actions and its ties with government's Washington worries about risk

00:07:29.575 --> 00:07:35.535
U.S. interests, and he accused South Africa of barriers on farm access, regulation, investment

00:07:35.535 --> 00:07:37.355
protection, and intellectual property.

00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:42.215
Trade Minister Park's Tau called the decision unfortunate, said the new issues were not

00:07:42.215 --> 00:07:47.355
part of talks that started in 2025, and said South Africa will push export markets wider

00:07:47.355 --> 00:07:48.195
to protect jobs.

00:07:49.311 --> 00:07:54.391
Figures he cited put ordinary most-favored nation terms on about 89 percent of South African

00:07:54.391 --> 00:08:00.411
exports to the United States in 2025, and a goa on about 10 percent, down from 28 percent

00:08:00.411 --> 00:08:07.471
in 2024. The value under the program fell to about $1.7 billion in 2025, from $4 billion

00:08:07.471 --> 00:08:14.131
the year before. Two-way trade reached $28.8 billion in 2025, and more than 600 American

00:08:14.131 --> 00:08:21.691
companies in South Africa support about 134,600 jobs. Pretoria says it supplies 12 of the 50 minerals

00:08:21.691 --> 00:08:27.291
Washington calls critical and 70% of American isotopes used among other things in cancer treatment

00:08:27.291 --> 00:08:31.611
and that its factories use American parts and vehicles and boats shipped under a goa.

00:08:32.091 --> 00:08:36.411
Ambassador Leo Brent Bozel, the third, wrote that South Africa's exit was regrettable,

00:08:36.751 --> 00:08:41.631
predictable, and preventable after the government turned down U.S. concerns. For Rwanda,

00:08:42.131 --> 00:08:47.051
Washington also raised human rights, political pluralism, the rule of law, and workers' rights.

00:08:47.051 --> 00:08:52.151
The BBC said relations were already strained, and that last year Trump accused South Africa

00:08:52.151 --> 00:08:56.891
of persecuting its white minority, opened an asylum route for white Afro-Connors, and

00:08:56.891 --> 00:09:00.031
repeated genocide claims the BBC called widely discredited.

00:09:01.169 --> 00:09:05.289
Hong Kong closed the main day of its global financial leaders investment summit on Tuesday.

00:09:05.849 --> 00:09:10.989
The Hong Kong Monetary Authority said, about 280 financial leaders were there, including

00:09:10.989 --> 00:09:17.369
around 120 group chairs in chief executives from banks, securities firms, asset owners and managers,

00:09:17.869 --> 00:09:23.329
private equity, venture capital, hedge funds and insurers. The theme is rethinking the playbook.

00:09:23.789 --> 00:09:28.409
Vice premier Healey Feng opened by video. Chief Executive John Lee gave a keynote.

00:09:28.929 --> 00:09:34.389
Financial Secretary Paul Chan spoke. HKMA Chief Eddie UA said this is the fifth year running,

00:09:34.629 --> 00:09:38.889
and that guests could see the city using innovation and technology while it holds its place

00:09:38.889 --> 00:09:43.009
as an international financial center. Panels asked whether the old financial

00:09:43.009 --> 00:09:47.389
playbook still works when risk is constant. The South China Morning Post reported

00:09:47.389 --> 00:09:51.649
that bankers voice confidence in Hong Kong as a bridge to mainland China and as

00:09:51.649 --> 00:09:57.189
a safe haven while capital flows shift. Jean Lamir, chairman of BNP Paribas, said

00:09:57.189 --> 00:10:00.989
European firms in Asia are looking harder for local funding and for tools to

00:10:00.989 --> 00:10:05.229
hedge currencies. The gathering started Monday with dinner at the Henderson and

00:10:05.229 --> 00:10:08.689
ends Wednesday with an investor forum run with the securities and futures

00:10:08.689 --> 00:10:13.669
Commission and the Hong Kong Academy of Finance. The HKMA live streamed the session.

00:10:14.731 --> 00:10:18.951
In Sudan, the United Nations says drones are this year's top killer of civilians.

00:10:19.391 --> 00:10:23.111
In a population already hit by famine and drought, the New York Times reports.

00:10:23.771 --> 00:10:28.711
Lebanon has cut power to public bodies as political disputes in war deep in the electricity crisis.

00:10:29.151 --> 00:10:36.191
Al Jazeera reports. Saudi Aramco said third-quarter profit rose 34 percent to 36.25 billion dollars

00:10:36.191 --> 00:10:39.811
despite houthi attacks on its sites, France 24 reports.

00:10:40.231 --> 00:10:42.671
California voters are deciding Proposition 40,

00:10:43.071 --> 00:10:46.071
a one-time 5% tax on net worth above $1 billion,

00:10:46.751 --> 00:10:50.231
with most of the money aimed at healthcare, France 24 reports.

00:10:50.691 --> 00:10:53.671
About 900 people on Campobello Island and New Brunswick

00:10:53.671 --> 00:10:56.531
reach the Canadian mainland only by a bridge into Maine,

00:10:57.051 --> 00:11:00.051
and tariffs have shut a local brewery, global news reports.

00:11:00.491 --> 00:11:04.071
On the case on both sides of ending a goa for South Africa and Rwanda,

00:11:04.071 --> 00:11:08.631
The decision is whether those two countries keep duty-free access for thousands of products,

00:11:09.011 --> 00:11:13.251
and Trump has told Congress he intends to end it on the 1st of January, 2027.

00:11:13.851 --> 00:11:16.791
That notice is an intention, not a change already in force.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:23.160
Greer's case is the annual review, practices that fail the eligibility test, corruption named

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:28.360
for South Africa, trade barriers and Trump's letter to Ramaphosa, and for Rwanda Human Rights,

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.220
pluralism, the rule of law and workers' rights.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:35.880
Boselle's line is that South Africa's loss was preventable if those concerns had been

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:36.200
met.

00:11:37.106 --> 00:11:39.586
Tau's case is that the penalty does not match the trade.

00:11:39.926 --> 00:11:44.906
He called it unfortunate, said the issues were new to talks begun in 2025, and pointed

00:11:44.906 --> 00:11:49.926
to a go-ah covering about a tenth of exports to the United States last year, about $1.7

00:11:49.926 --> 00:11:56.066
billion, against $28.8 billion in two-way trade, plus critical minerals and medical isotopes.

00:11:56.586 --> 00:11:59.966
The date written into the notice is the 1st of January, 2027.

00:11:59.966 --> 00:12:05.546
A sign of progress, Warsaw Modeling Airport in Poland is operating again after a bomb threat

00:12:05.546 --> 00:12:10.106
